{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sports and Leisure"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Baseball Star"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situation"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le02ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Stressing Two Syllables Back From the Suffix: -acy"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you say words that end with the suffix -acy, you stress the third syllable from the end of the word, or two syllables before the -cy ending."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read these words out loud. Concentrate on the pronunciation. Stress the third syllable from the end."}, {"type": "text", "content": "democracy<br/> legacy<br/> meritocracy<br/> hypocrisy"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Of course, I have to think about my legacy. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The best thing about baseball is that it's a meritocracy."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Stress for Nouns and Adjectives "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You stress nouns and adjectives in a sentence to add meaning or emphasis to a statement or a message."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English, 2-syllable adjectives or words usually have stress on the first syllable.<br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">awe</span>some, <span class=\"strong\">pre</span>sent, <span class=\"strong\">cle</span>ver, <span class=\"strong\">foot</span>ball, <span class=\"strong\">base</span>ball</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For compound nouns, the stress is on the first part of the noun.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">green</span>house, <span class=\"strong\">baske</span>tball, v<span class=\"strong\">olley</span>ball</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For compound adjectives, the stress is on the second part of the noun.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">old-<span class=\"strong\">fash</span>ioned, bad-<span class=\"strong\">temp</span>ered</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use an adjective to describe a noun, you normally emphasize the noun if you are not stressing the quality of the noun.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I drive a red <span class=\"strong\">car</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to emphasize the quality of that noun, you stress the adjective that describes it.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look at that <span class=\"strong\">red</span> car over there!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you have several adjectives describing a noun, you stress the quality that you are focusing on the most.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'm driving a brand new red <span class=\"strong\">Japanese</span> car. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm here with legendary star Tip O'Neill. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Not at all, you're more of a bad-tempered young curmudgeon."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What are some things every baseball fan should know?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "literacy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to read and write"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I mean, you have to have some literacy when it comes to the jargon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you when conducting an interview with an athlete."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "doubleheader"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when two (usually sporting) events are held in the same day\t"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If someone says we got a doubleheader, it means we're playing two games in one day. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "southpaw"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is left handed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Or if someone says there's a southpaw pitching today, it means he's left-handed."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "meritocracy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where everyone is judged on merit and ability"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The best thing about baseball is that it's a meritocracy. You can't fake the stats. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accuracy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "precision "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They can measure this stuff with high levels of accuracy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legitimacy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the quality of being legal or verified"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It gives everything we do a legitimacy, because we can measure our value in so many different ways."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "advocacy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "public support of an idea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It took a lot of advocacy to change people's attitudes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "delicacy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a delicious food, usually one that is uncommon and expensive\t"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Chewing tobacco used to be considered a delicacy in the dugout."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dugout"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a shelter, usually located partially underground, for members of a sports team\t"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The visiting team was assigned the eastern dugout."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legacy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "what a person leaves behind after moving on or passing away"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Of course, I have to think about my legacy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob04aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose your favorite athlete."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a list of twenty questions to ask."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Have a partner read the questions to you. Invent the answers yourself."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research an athlete."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create questions that could be used in an interview."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I respond to interview questions."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can say and use words like <span class=\"italic\">accuracy</span> and <span class=\"italic\">legitimacy</span>."}, {"type": "Learn